Linter: deferred lambdas in a string annotation lost the parsed annotation tokens, so F632
looked up annotation-relative ranges in the file tokens and panicked.
Regression test included; fuzz repro: repro/fix-linter-deferred-lambda-annotation.py (ruff_fix_validity).

diff --git a/crates/ruff_linter/resources/test/fixtures/pyflakes/F632.py b/crates/ruff_linter/resources/test/fixtures/pyflakes/F632.py
index ce1fe2decdee2303ecea02e121248ff7c281adc8..18c87c36ba4b6929ff98ed71ea17ceca7e75aa21 100644
--- a/crates/ruff_linter/resources/test/fixtures/pyflakes/F632.py
+++ b/crates/ruff_linter/resources/test/fixtures/pyflakes/F632.py
@@ -32,3 +32,7 @@ if values[1is not None ] is not '-':
 
 # Regression test for https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/11736
 variable: "123 is not y"
+
+# A lambda in a string annotation is visited after the annotation: its fix still needs
+# the tokens of the parsed annotation.
+x: "lambda: 0 is ()"
